From 53ffc07b2450f1ea5ee2bab32f8ab80819a5c83f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 07:00:20 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Elwynn's own light: the new look re-lights the forest by time
 of day (worldLook)

The new look starts here, WoW Forever's way: 1.12's models and textures kept, the light and colour
hand-tuned zone by zone over Light.dbc. In Elwynn Forest the light now runs warm against cool
shadows through the day: a rose first light with the morning mist, clear far views at noon, a
golden hour, a violet dusk and a brighter blue night. Each key of the table nudges the sampled
light (sun, ambient, fog and all five sky stops get a tint at their own weight, and the fog end
a multiplier), smoothstepped between keys across the whole game day; the same table carries the
values the later full-screen pass reads (saturation, contrast, warmth, bloom, mist and rays).

The grade comes in over 3 s on entering Elwynn, from any of its sub-zones (Goldshire, Northshire
and the rest, resolved to zone 12 through AreaTable's parents), and goes over 3 s on leaving, so
the border never snaps. Under water and as a ghost the reference's own atmospheres keep the
screen. A new CVar, `worldLook` (default 1), switches all of it: `worldLook 0` is 1.12's look
exactly, so the two can be compared side by side.
